variable {d : ℕ}

/-! ## Lattices -/

/-- The rescaled lattice `hℤ^d ⊆ ℝ^d`. -/
def scaledLattice (d : ℕ) (h : ℝ) : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) :=
  {x | ∀ i, ∃ n : ℤ, x i = n * h}

/-- The lattice `ℤ^d ⊆ ℝ^d`. -/
def lattice (d : ℕ) : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) := scaledLattice d 1

/-! ## Lattice points in a bounded region

Needed to make "maximal size" in Definition 5.11 meaningful, and to pick the
axis of Lemma 3.3. -/

/-! ## The half-closed cubes tile `ℝ^d`

"For technical reasons, we need the property that every `x` in `ℝ^d` is
contained in some cube. Therefore we consider half-closed cubes." The cubes
`Ã_h(x)`, `x ∈ hℤ^d`, do tile: every point lies in exactly one. -/

